    id: "44c355b694cfa3fe16e2",
    cat: "conflitti",
    title: "Israeli strike on motorcycle kills Palestinian in Gaza City, injures child",
    summary: "Separate attacks struck central refugee camps as officials warned Gaza's health sector faces total collapse.",
    preview: "Separate attacks struck central refugee camps as officials warned Gaza’s health sector faces total collapse. An Israeli air strike on a motorcycle has killed one Palestinian and injured others, with one child in critical condition, according to Palestinian media reports. The attack targeted the vehicle in the Sheikh Radwan neighbourhood, west of Gaza City, on Friday, Wafa news agency reported. Ongoing Israeli strikes on the besieged enclave have killed at least 1,381 people since a “ceasefire” between Israel and Hamas was announced in October 2025.",
    body: "Separate attacks struck central refugee camps as officials warned Gaza’s health sector faces total collapse.\n\nAn Israeli air strike on a motorcycle has killed one Palestinian and injured others, with one child in critical condition, according to Palestinian media reports.\n\nThe attack targeted the vehicle in the Sheikh Radwan neighbourhood, west of Gaza City, on Friday, Wafa news agency reported. Ongoing Israeli strikes on the besieged enclave have killed at least 1,381 people since a “ceasefire” between Israel and Hamas was announced in October 2025.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Macklemore pledges $1m in tour earnings to Palestinian groups\n\n- list 2 of 3UK court clears woman of voicing support for Hamas in university speech\n\n- list 3 of 3Israel is killing the people who could end its wars\n\nIsrael has killed at least 73,795 people and wounded 174,869 others since the start of its genocidal war against Palestinians in Gaza in October 2023.\n\nOn Friday, the Israeli army also opened fire in the Nuseirat and al-Bureij refugee camps in the central Gaza Strip, according to Wafa. The attacks on tents sheltering displaced people have resulted in multiple injuries.\n\nEarlier this week, an Israeli “double-tap” air strike killed a paramedic and a 15-year-old schoolboy in Gaza City. Israeli forces claimed they were targeting Hamas operatives.\n\nLast month, UNICEF found that, on average, one child is killed a day by Israel.\n\nFamilies are now confined to about a third of the enclave, sheltering among destroyed buildings, rubble and uncleared waste, the agency said.\n\nOn Wednesday, a previously damaged building collapsed in Gaza City, killing at least 21 people, including 12 children. The Palestinian Civil Defence agency in Gaza struggled to recover bodies from under the rubble due to Israel’s severe restrictions on heavy equipment.\n\nThe Health Ministry warned on Wednesday that Gaza’s health system was on the verge of “total collapse” as Israel continues to limit the amount of medical aid and fuel permitted to enter the enclave.",
    content_status: "full",
    source: "Al Jazeera",
    url: "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/19/israeli-strike-on-motorcycle-in-gaza-city-kills-one-injures-child?traffic_source=rss",
    time: "5 ore fa",
